{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-7781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+8y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-7781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+6\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+8{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +8=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +4)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =-4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-7781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "356f2556c7b72e1c7de6ef178888a55add1b49d09ea1275773381146e73b825a"} {"question" "q-7781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-7781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{6x}+B{e}^{8x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-7781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-4x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(x)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-3y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-2\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}-3{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -3)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-1$ or $\\lambda =3.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-x}$ and ${e}^{3x}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-5{e}^{-3x}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "356f2556c7b72e1c7de6ef178888a55add1b49d09ea1275773381146e73b825a"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "-5{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "2{e}^{-x}+4{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "8{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "{e}^{3x}-3{e}^{-x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5{e}^{-3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=y(t)$ satisfies the equation ${y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-4y=0,$ which of the following **cannot** be $y(t)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda t}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda t}+3\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda t}-4{e}^{\\lambda t} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda t}({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so the solutions of the auxiliary equation  are $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =1.$\n\nTherefore, any linear combination of the functions ${e}^{-4t}$ and ${e}^{t}$ is a solution to the original differential equation. \n\nAmong the given options, only $-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}$ is not a solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "356f2556c7b72e1c7de6ef178888a55add1b49d09ea1275773381146e73b825a"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-5{e}^{-4t}"] ["math" "-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}"] ["math" "2{e}^{t}"] ["math" "4{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{t}"] ["math" "{e}^{-4t}-{e}^{t}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-64707" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-{e}^{-4t}+{e}^{-t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-11\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+28y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-11\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+28{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-11\\lambda +28) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-11\\lambda +28=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -7)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =4$ or $\\lambda =7.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{7x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "356f2556c7b72e1c7de6ef178888a55add1b49d09ea1275773381146e73b825a"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=A{e}^{-14x}+B{e}^{-2x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{-7x}+B{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{14x}"] ["math" "y=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{7x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-90722" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=A{e}^{4x}+B{e}^{7x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-130118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-5\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3afd4a96145533dc273a3"} {"question" "q-130118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $y={e}^{\\lambda x}.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}-5\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+4{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4=0.\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0,\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =1$ or $\\lambda =4.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070449/state.json" "file_sha256" "cfc38f3d054037f51d1bb5fe5581c267eeac7a0224b3a